  0. Definitions.

  "This License" refers to version 3 of the GNU General Public License.

  "The Program" refers to any copyrightable work licensed under this
License.  Each licensee is addressed as "you".  "Licensees" and
"recipients" may be individuals or organizations.

  To "modify" a work means to copy from or adapt all or part of the
work in a fashion requiring copyright permission, other than the making of
an exact copy.  The resulting work is called a "modified version" of the
earlier work or a work "based on" the earlier work.

  A "covered work" means either the unmodified Program or a work based
on the Program.

  To "propagate" a work means to do anything with it that, without
permission, would make you infringe under applicable copyright law, other
than executing it on a computer or making minor, insignificant changes.
Propagation includes copying (with or without making it available to
the public), distribution (with or without modification), making
available to the public, and in some countries other activities as well.

  To "convey" a work means any kind of propagation that enables other
parties to make or propagate the work.  Mere interaction with a computer
through a user interface does not convey a work.

  An interactive user interface displays "Appropriate Legal Notices"
to the extent that it includes a convenient and prominent feature that
(1) displays an appropriate copyright notice, and (2) tells the user
that there is no warranty for the work (except to the extent that
warranties are provided), that licensees may redistribute the work under
this License, and how to view a copy of this License.  If the interface
presents a user-defined list of commands or options, such as a menu, a
large command button in the menu meets this criterion.

